diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 6c8651b..672b1e3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -16,6 +16,14 @@ The `types` package exposes a `types.PacketConn` interface type. This is a super
 
 The `network` package implements all of the important routing logic. Packets sent over the `network.PacketConn` are unencrypted, unsigned, and otherwise at least as insecure as UDP. The main use case for this package is to wrap it with a more secure protocol (e.g. DTLS, QUIC, or TLS-over-μTP).
 
+A local `SendLookup` can precede fresh-peer routing convergence. Explicit
+lookups receive at most two automatic retries from the existing maintenance
+cycle, respecting the configured path throttle (with a one-second floor).
+Retries neither extend the rumor lifetime nor allocate another timer or packet
+buffer, and an accepted signed path notification cancels them. The caller's
+original buffering and best-effort delivery semantics remain unchanged; this
+is not a guarantee that every initial datagram is delivered.
+
 Internally, protocol traffic is signed (when necessary for authentication), but never encrypted, so this should be legal in environments where encryption is not permissible (e.g. amateur radio networks).
 
 ### Signed
